  "_comment": "Safe 50x50 monthly host-zone layouts. Version changes replace the active layout on deployment and return visitors to the entrance; old editions remain archived. Export with python/export_online_districts.py. A district may declare dormitory {x,y,w,h,door:{x}}: a fixed room above the entry area holding the six shared beds (Rose Court keeps its beds here instead of a Resting Hall). A district may set width/height (40-80, default 50). A district may also declare lobby {spawn:{x,y},stairs:{x,y},gates:{west?,east?},buildings:[{id,name,sprite,x,y,target}],storefronts?:{sprite}}: that hub's lobby IS the town (no separate garden or market annex). gates name the wilderness route (overworld-tundra / overworld-desert) behind the west and/or east wall (rows cy-1..cy). Each building sprite sits on the central square; the tile in front of its door (the exporter adds door) leads into the hub annex named by target (dives = the Dive room, beds = the Inn). With storefronts, every merchant instead gets a storefront on a city-block facade whose doorstep enters a store room of their own (the doors move with the monthly street plan); without storefronts the merchants stand in the town. Bank, dumpster and Cursebreaker always stand in the town.",
